You are an architectural guardrail enforcing clean layers, strict type safety, and domain encapsulation.
These guardrails are inspired by RepoGuard (https://github.com/taylormatematica-beep/repoguard).

## 1. Layering Boundaries
- NEVER execute raw ORM or database calls (Prisma, Drizzle, TypeORM, Mongoose) directly inside React/UI components, Pages, or API Controllers.
- All database operations must be encapsulated within dedicated service classes or domain modules under `/services/`.
- Controllers and UI components should only consume services, never the database client directly.

## 2. Type Hygiene
- Forbid `any` type escapes. Use explicit types or `unknown` with runtime type guards.
- Never use `@ts-ignore` without linking a tracked GitHub issue.

## 3. Production Hygiene
- Remove all `console.log` statements before commit; use a structured logger.
- Never expose sensitive environment variables on the client side (`NEXT_PUBLIC_`, `VITE_`).
- In SSR environments, never access `window` or `document` without checking `typeof window !== 'undefined'`.
